  <prompt>Add three optional, generic seams to the shared Spaarke DataGrid: a host-supplied row source, a host row-actions column (wiring the unused onRecordAction), and an opt-in ellipsis-with-tooltip for truncated text cells. With none of them passed, every existing grid renders and behaves exactly as today.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Fluent UI v9. Owner of the change to the shared DataGrid on behalf of the dataset-grid framework owners (owner approval 2026-11-22).</role>
  <goal>A host can give the grid its rows (paged, with lazy scroll), its per-row actions (hidden per row when not allowed) and opt cells into ellipsis + tooltip, while columns, labels and renderers still come from the grid configuration; every other consumer is unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design: `projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-023-design.md` §2–§3.1 (binding). Today rows come only from FetchXML through `IDataverseClient` → `useLazyLoad` (`DataGrid/useLazyLoad.ts`); `onRecordAction` is destructured as `_onRecordAction` and never used (`DataGrid.tsx` ~:1209); `overrides.columnRenderers` replaces only cells of configured columns (~:1236). Config load + `resolveConfig` (`configResolution.ts:252`) stay the source of columns. Resize is native, widths fitted to the container (~:1260-1310). `DisplayConfig` lives in `src/types/DataGridConfiguration.ts:83`. Inside the external SPA the grid is mounted only via `widgets/ExternalDataGrid.tsx`, which forwards all props (do not edit it). Task 032 later adds persisted widths/sort on top: keep sort inside the grid.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/index.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/DataGridConfiguration.ts</file>
      <file role="create">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/useHostRowSource.ts (or extend useLazyLoad; choose the smaller diff)</file>
      <file role="create">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.rowSource.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="create">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.rowActions.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="create">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.truncateTooltip.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.hostCommands.test.tsx (how the last additive host option was added and tested)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/CommandBar.tsx (DataGridHostCommand shape)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Every new prop is optional; no Xrm, no fetching, no entity-name literals in the shared lib; types exported from the DataGrid index (and the package barrel if DataGridHostCommand is exported there).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §3.1">`rowSource(req: { page, pageSize, signal }) → Promise&lt;{ rows, hasMore, truncated? }&gt;`. When given, the grid runs no FetchXML query (no retrieveMultipleRecords call), no chips and no host-filter overlay; it still loads the configuration and entity metadata. `rowSourceKey` change reloads page 1. A rejected page shows the grid's existing error banner. Paging uses the existing sentinel / lazy scroll (ADR-051); `truncated: true` shows a notice.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §3.1, FR-07">`rowActions: { id, label, icon, isVisible?(record) }[]`; rendered as a final fixed-width, non-resizable column of icon buttons (tooltip = aria-label = label) that call `onRecordAction(id, recordId, record, ctx)`. An action whose `isVisible` returns false is NOT rendered (hide, don't disable). Above an inline limit, the rest fold into a "More actions" menu. No column when `rowActions` is absent or empty.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §3.1, ADR-021">Truncate-with-tooltip is opt-in (`display.truncateWithTooltip` on the configuration, or a `truncateWithTooltip` prop): text cells ellipsise, and a cell whose content overflows shows a Fluent `Tooltip` with the full text. Off by default.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012, 34 consumers">With none of the new props/config passed, rendering, data loading, sort and resize are unchanged — a test proves it for each seam (must-not-fire pair).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">React-16-safe hooks only in anything `pcf-safe` exports (no useId / useSyncExternalStore / useTransition).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 only; semantic tokens; no hard-coded colours.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No SPA, BFF or Dataverse change in this task; `ExternalDataGrid.tsx` not edited.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-023-design.md</file>
