  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load knowledge; declare rigor and model tier (task-execute Step 0.5).</step>
    <step order="1">Add the types (`DataGridRowSource`, `DataGridRowSourceRequest/Result`, `DataGridRowAction`, `DisplayConfig.truncateWithTooltip`) and export them.</step>
    <step order="2">Row source: route the grid's records/isLoading/hasMore/error/fetchNextPage through the host loader when `rowSource` is given; keep the FetchXML path byte-for-byte otherwise. Abort in-flight requests on unmount and on `rowSourceKey` change.</step>
    <step order="3">Row actions: wire `onRecordAction`; append the actions column; per-row visibility; overflow menu.</step>
    <step order="4">Truncate-with-tooltip in text cells (default renderer and primary-name link) when enabled.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: must-fire and must-not-fire for each seam (rowSource: no retrieveMultipleRecords call, pages appended, key reload, error banner, truncated notice; without it: FetchXML path unchanged. rowActions: hidden per row, click calls onRecordAction with id/record, no column when absent. Tooltip: shown on overflow when on; absent when off).</step>
    <step order="6">Run the whole shared-lib test suite and its build (`npm run build` in Spaarke.UI.Components); run the external SPA's tests and build (it consumes the lib by path).</step>
    <step order="7">Update docs/architecture/SPAARKE-DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-ARCHITECTURE.md with the three host options (short section). Task status: POML + TASK-INDEX, `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`; notes in `notes/task-023-notes.md`.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.rowSource.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.rowActions.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.truncateTooltip.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/architecture/SPAARKE-DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-ARCHITECTURE.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">With `rowSource`, the grid shows the host's rows with the configuration's columns, loads further pages on scroll, reloads on `rowSourceKey` change, shows the error banner on a rejected page and a notice on `truncated`, and never calls `retrieveMultipleRecords`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With `rowActions`, each row shows only the actions whose `isVisible` is not false; clicking one calls `onRecordAction(id, recordId, record, ctx)`; each button's tooltip equals its aria-label.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With truncate-with-tooltip on, an overflowing cell ellipsises and shows its full text in a tooltip; with it off, cells render as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With none of the new options, existing DataGrid tests pass unchanged and a must-not-fire test shows the FetchXML path, columns and absence of an actions column are as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Shared-lib build and full test suite pass; external SPA build and tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Split from task 023 by owner decision 2026-11-22 (design B+C+D). 023b and 023c follow. Approval for the dataset-grid owners: owner, 2026-11-22.</notes>

